Run the packaged Lemonade and FastFlowLM for the NPU in a Gentoo system
install.

Enabling the NPU makes Studio download a pinned FastFlowLM, either
directly (the default since 2026.11.8, with flm_host.py standing in for
lemond) or through Lemonade's Ubuntu build in ~/.unsloth/studio/lemonade
(UNSLOTH_NPU_LEMONADE=1), and it looks for the binaries only there.
With UNSLOTH_STUDIO_SYSTEM=1 (set
by the unsloth-studio wrapper and by unsloth-desktop) it now uses
/usr/bin/lemond from sci-ml/lemonade and /opt/fastflowlm/bin/flm from
sci-ml/fastflowlm, overridable with UNSLOTH_STUDIO_LEMOND and
UNSLOTH_STUDIO_FLM. The private lemond config names that flm in
flm.npu_bin, so lemond runs it instead of downloading one, and Enable
skips lemond's FastFlowLM install and the check against Unsloth's
pinned FastFlowLM version. Studio's own config, cache and model
directories are kept.

